Getsome wrote:
>
> I'm having a hard time figuring out the weapon charts
> http://www.steelypips.org/nethack/341/weap-341.html
> It would seem that only a Quarterstaff & a Dagger are good weapons for a
> Wizard?
> What weapon should I be looking for?

The best weapon for a wizard is a concept not an object -
combat at range.  You want attack spells, wand zaps and
missiles more than you want the third-string-backup of
melee attacks.  The monster that dies well away from you
is every bit as dead as the one whose breath you could
smell when you whacked it.

That said, it's my opinion that many of the objects and
object classes in Nethack are there as much for distraction
as for best use.  Quarterstaffs for other than healer are a
distraction to me.  It's tempting to #enhance your skills in
it, but doing that wastes slots that you will need later.
Don't.  Use as many slots as you can on your spell schools.
Advance dagger to Expert soonest, but throw them far
more often than melee with them.  For meaner weapons
consider only advancing a very mean one.  Greyswandir,
the Brands, any of the crowning weapons.  For anything
less, save that for after you've ascended your first wizard.



